Layout rebalance — screenshot audit findings F5/F6. Pure CSS, theme.py only.
Apply AFTER 0006, against the LOCAL tree:

    git apply handoff/0007-layout-rebalance.patch
    # fallback: patch -p1 -l < handoff/0007-layout-rebalance.patch

Contents
  R1  #panel-services 3fr -> 2fr: the services grid was holding 3 rows in a
      ~15-row panel; the freed third goes to the lower band
  R2  #lower-band 2fr -> 3fr: methodology + notes (the text-heavy panels)
      get the reclaimed space
  R3  #loot-cards-container fixed 9 rows -> auto (max 12): the flags card
      stopped wrapping its hint, the empty foothold/privesc cards stop
      squatting on the Intel station
  R4  .loot-box height 9 -> auto (same rationale; the copy in widgets.py
      DEFAULT_CSS keeps losing priority to APP_CSS, no edit needed there)

Note: F1 (emoji tofu) is handled by dev/emoji_purge.py, not this patch —
emoji bytes are more reliable via scripted replacement than diff context.

